Evans' RT3: polarized doubling-adding radiative transfer for a plane-parallel
medium of randomly oriented particles with a plane of symmetry, with solar
(direct beam) and thermal sources, all Fourier azimuth modes and NSTOKES 1 to
4.  K. F. Evans and G. L. Stephens, 1991: "A New Polarized Atmospheric
Radiative Transfer Model", J. Quant. Spectrosc. Radiat. Transfer 46, 413-423.

Source: PolRadTran.tar from https://nit.coloradolinux.com/polrad.html
(sha256 7b0eff794319330321e27a6f312588a289ed080bb266500dcecf485f6a7cff9d),
MIT licence (../LICENSE).  ARTS 2 never shipped RT3; ARTS 3 uses it only as
an external reference for other solvers (src/core/rt3), with no workspace
layer.

Files:

  radtran3.f, radscat3.f, radintg3.f, radutil3.f
                  the RADTRAN subroutine and its routines, modified as below
                  (built)
  *.orig          the four files above as in the tar
  rt3.f           Evans' main program (file input and output), unchanged
                  and not built; its OUTPUT_FILE shows how the Fourier
                  series is summed
  runmietest      Evans' Mie benchmark script (the case of the 1991 paper),
                  with the scattering file and the expected output
                  mietest.out.check; unchanged, not run
  runtesta        Evans' general test script (Rayleigh + Mie layers, solar
                  and thermal), with testa.out.check; unchanged, not run
  rt3_c_interface.f90
                  ISO_C_BINDING entry points (new)
  CMakeLists.txt  builds the library rt3 (ENABLE_RT3)

The matrix routines are the shared ../radmat.f.  The two benchmark tables are
compared with the ARTS build in src/core/rt3/test/rt3-test.cpp and
tests/core/rt3/closed-form.rt3.py.

ARTS3 changes, each marked with a "c ARTS3:" comment in the source:

- In-memory scattering properties (radtran3.f, radscat3.f).  RADTRAN takes
  NSL scattering sets (SCAT_EXTINCT, SCAT_SCATTER, SCAT_NLEGEN and
  SCAT_COEF(6,LDCOEF,NSL), the six columns of a scattering file for
  L = 0 .. SCAT_NLEGEN) and the 1-based set of each layer, SCATLAYERS (0 for
  no scattering), instead of the file names SCAT_FILES.  Each set is
  processed once, in set order (RT3 processed every new file in layer
  order).  READ_SCAT_FILE is replaced by GET_SCAT_SET, which copies a set and
  applies READ_SCAT_FILE's delta-M scaling unchanged.  With delta-M the
  scaling reads the coefficients up to L = 2*NUMMU even when the series is
  shorter; READ_SCAT_FILE read entries there that the file never set (left
  from an earlier file, or uninitialised), GET_SCAT_SET sets them to zero.
  The check NLEGEN < MAXLEG now precedes the copy (RT3 checked
  after reading, one coefficient too late).  New STOPs: NSL > MAXLAY, and
  the direct-beam buffer for NSL sets.  The truncation message names the
  set number instead of the file.  NOUTLEVELS/OUTLEVELS are unchanged.
- Symbol clashes with RT4 (radintg3.f, radscat3.f, radutil3.f,
  radtran3.f).  The routines that RT4 also defines carry an RT3_ prefix:
  CHECK_NORM, COMBINE_LAYERS, DOUBLE_GAUSS_QUADRATURE, DOUBLING_INTEGRATION,
  FRESNEL_RADIANCE, FRESNEL_SURFACE, GAUSS_LEGENDRE_QUADRATURE, INITIALIZE,
  INITIAL_SOURCE, INTERNAL_RADIANCE, LAMBERT_RADIANCE, LAMBERT_SURFACE,
  LOBATTO_QUADRATURE, NONSCATTER_LAYER, PLANCK_FUNCTION, THERMAL_RADIANCE,
  and the COMMON blocks /SCRATCH1/ and /SCRATCH2/ are /RT3_SCRATCH1/ and
  /RT3_SCRATCH2/ (with the same names, RT3 and RT4 would share the scratch
  memory).  Two calls are wrapped onto a continuation line to stay within
  column 72; no original code line extends beyond column 72.  librt3 and
  librt4 export no common symbol.
- radutil3.f RT3_PLANCK_FUNCTION: the 5-digit radiation constants 1.1911D8
  and 1.4388D4 are replaced by the exact-SI values used in ../rt4.  At 3 um
  and 300-200 K this raises B by 2.1e-4 to 3.4e-4 relative.
- rt3_c_interface.f90 (new): rt3_radtran and the three quadratures with
  explicit C types (int64_t scalars and index arrays, one-character flags by
  value, the complex ground index as two doubles).

Nothing else is changed.  The remaining STOPs (array limits, the Legendre
normalisation check, the FFT size) are checked by the C++ wrapper before
the call; see src/core/rt3/rt3.h and doc/arts/dev.rt3.rst.
